Subject: An empty program is not a threaded one

What this does
  An empty program is not a threaded one.

Why we need it
  `regvm_code_all_threaded` formed `p + len` before checking the pointer, so the refusal path -- which leaves `regvm_code` NULL and `len` 0, and which the baseline tier makes routine -- applied a zero offset to a null pointer. Undefined behaviour.

What it adds
  An explicit `code == NULL \.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
